  "knowledgePattern": "Count bounded integer allocations without distinguishing identical objects",
  "knowledgeTags": [
    "counting"
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Let A, B and C be the numbers of balls in the three labelled boxes. Each lies between 0 and 4, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>If A is 0, only B = 4 works. If A is 1, B can be 3 or 4. If A is 2, B can be 2, 3 or 4. If A is 3, B can be 1, 2, 3 or 4. If A is 4, B can be 0, 1, 2, 3 or 4. In every case, C is fixed by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p>The total is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>. Each allocation appears once because its A and B values identify its row. Answer E.</p>",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Fix the first box",
      "body": "<p>Call the boxes A, B and C. Start with A empty. List the allowed numbers in B; the number in C is then whatever is needed to make 8 balls.</p>",
      "recap": "Once two box counts are fixed, the total fixes the third.",
      "pitfall": "Empty boxes are allowed, but no box may hold more than 4.",
      "pause": "List the valid choices when A has no balls.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b1-l09",
          "reminder": "Once two box counts are fixed, the total fixes the third."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Make the list in order",
      "body": "<p>Repeat with A holding 1, 2, 3 and then 4 balls. For each row, keep only choices where both B and C hold between 0 and 4.</p>",
      "recap": "An ordered list helps you find every case without repeating one.",
      "pitfall": "The boxes are different, even though the balls are identical.",
      "pause": "Count the valid rows in your table.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b1-l09",
          "reminder": "An ordered list helps you find every case without repeating one."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
